course: dictionary
lesson: 2509
title: Months and context clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a month, and the words around it give you clues about which one. In «Kiritimati ... it's still 10 am on 31 December in London», the number 31 is a clue: December has 31 days.
explain: Context also tells you about the season. In «So when Freddie in England has a cold Christmas, his cousin in Australia is at the beach in his togs», a cold Christmas and a day at the beach show that December is winter in one place and summer in another.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does December fit as the twelfth month, the one that comes after November? If it does, you have understood it.
fact: December is the twelfth and last month of the year.
fact: December has 31 days, comes after November, and is followed by January.
fact: In the north, such as the UK, USA and Canada, December is in winter.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, December is in summer.
exercise: Which month comes right after November? | March | *December | January | October
exercise: Jack says «Stinkin' hot arvo, mate» in Sydney in December. What season is it there? | Winter | Autumn | *Summer | Spring
exercise: How many days does December have? | 30 | *31 | 29 | 28
test: In the UK, what season is December? | Autumn | *Winter | Summer | Spring
test: «It's still 10 am on 31 December in London.» What does the number 31 tell you about December? | It is the first month of the year | It comes before November | It is the shortest month | *It has 31 days
exam: Which sentence gives a clue that December is summer in one place? | The Geminids peak around 13 to 14 December | Freddie has a cold Christmas in England | *Jack is off to the beach in his togs, in a stinkin' hot arvo in Sydney | Ukraine made 25 December a state holiday
